## Summary

I shipped a production-polished native Apple (SwiftUI) parity of `components/ui/DataTableColumnsMenu.tsx` at `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/DataTableColumnsMenu.*` — **8 files** mirroring the accepted sibling 0210's split:

- **Adapter** (slug, `DataTableColumnsMenuColumn`/`Row`, layout metrics, pure `Projector`), **Model** (i18n facade P1/S10, telemetry P1/S11, `@Observable` controller P1/S8), **view** (popover + default "Columns" trigger), **Views** (Panel, Header w/ "Show all", RowView, checkbox ToggleStyle, friendly EmptyView), **Previews**, **.strings**, and **two test files** (pure projector + controller/view/strings).

**Parity decisions:** the web source is a controlled, storage-agnostic presentational primitive (only data source is `useTranslation`), so I reproduced its real branches — closed/open-with-columns/empty — plus a friendly empty state, and did **not** fabricate loading/error/stale/offline (no fetchable source), documenting this exactly as the sibling did. Unique `DataTableColumnsMenu*` type names avoid module redeclaration vs the singular sibling. All i18n via the facade; a11y labels on every control; once-only `view.opened`.

**Trustworthy verification — all green on this surface:**
- Swift 6 typecheck of the full dependency surface (iOS, against real design tokens) ✅
- Compilation **inside the real macOS whole-app module** (un-conflated, 0 source errors) ✅
- `swiftlint --strict`, `swiftformat --lint`, placeholder gate — **0** on my files ✅

